    "result": "The office products dataset is group `g1` (13,933 of 20,000 items have `main_cat = 'Office Products'`). Note `items_g1.avg_rtg` is the product's historical average, while `fdbk_g1` holds the individual review ratings — the question asks for \"review rating given to\" products, i.e. the ratings in the reviews table, joined to items priced over $50.\n\n```sql\nSELECT AVG(f.rtg) AS avg_review_rating\nFROM fdbk_g1 f\nJOIN items_g1 i ON i.ref_id = f.ref_id\nWHERE i.prc > 50;\n```\n\n**Result: 4.1054** (across 41,411 reviews of 1,192 office products priced over $50).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"answer\": 4.1054,\n  \"sql\": \"SELECT AVG(f.rtg) AS avg_review_rating FROM fdbk_g1 f JOIN items_g1 i ON i.ref_id = f.ref_id WHERE i.prc > 50;\"\n}\n```\n\nNote on interpretation: if instead you average each product's own average rating (`items_g1.avg_rtg`, equally weighting products rather than reviews), the result is 4.1178. Both interpretations land at ≈4.11; the value above follows the review-level reading of \"review rating.\"",
